{"step_index":179,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T15:00:50Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T17:00:50+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T17:00:50+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/prover_eval/reclassify.py`\nTotal Lines: 90\nTotal Bytes: 3875\nShowing lines 1 to 60\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: #!/usr/bin/env python\n2: \"\"\"tools/prover_eval/reclassify.py — separate real resolutions from formalization gaps.\n3: \n4: The evaluation design is explicit that `definition_gap` must never be collapsed\n5: into `formally_refuted`, and the harness had no such status — so four\n6: \"resolutions\" were reported as model successes when they were defects in the\n7: export:\n8: \n9:   * three exploited the missing `nontrivial` guard, refutable by `Fin 0` where\n10:     every `forall v` class predicate holds vacuously;\n11:   * one exploited `minCard` returning 0 for an invariant with no witness, which\n12:     turned `Z_c + 2 <= 2 * Z_t` into `2 <= 0`.\n13: \n14: A resolution counts as genuine only if the statement it refuted carried every\n15: guard its content requires. This reads the recorded results, checks each\n16: resolved item against the corrected challenge, and writes the split.\n17: \"\"\"\n18: from __future__ import annotations\n19: \n20: import glob, json, os, sys\n21: \n22: sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(\n23:     os.path.abspath(__file__)))))\n24: from pipeline.lean_disproof import PARTIAL_INVARIANTS  # noqa: E402\n25: \n26: \n27: def main() -> int:\n28:     # A single run is recorded twice — once by the live scorer (w16_*/f16_*) and\n29:     # once by the offline re-scorer (rescored_*). Keyed by (model, condition,\n30:     # item) so the same refutation is not counted as two.\n31:     out, index, seen = [], {}, set()\n32:     for p in (\"gold\", \"frontier\", \"development\"):\n33:         f = f\"benchmark/challenges_{p}/index.json\"\n34:         if os.path.exists(f):\n35:             for c in json.load(open(f)):\n36:                 index[c[\"id\"]] = (p, c)\n37: \n38:     for f in sorted(glob.glob(\"benchmark/rescored_*_*.json\")\n39:                     + glob.glob(\"benchmark/w16_*.json\")\n40:                     + glob.glob(\"benchmark/f16_*.json\")):\n41:         d = json.load(open(f))\n42:         resolved = d.get(\"resolved\") or {\n43:             r[\"id\"]: r[\"verified_direction\"] for r in d.get(\"results\", [])\n44:             if r.get(\"verified_direction\")}\n45:         for rid, direction in resolved.items():\n46:             if rid not in index:\n47:                 continue\n48:             part, c = index[rid]\n49:             stmt = c[\"statement\"]\n50:             needs_guard = \"nontrivial\" not in stmt\n51:             needs_defined = [n for n in PARTIAL_INVARIANTS if n in stmt]\n52:             # The recorded run used the pre-fix challenge; the corrected one is\n53:             # what decides whether the refutation had any content.\n54:             gap = needs_guard or bool(needs_defined)\n55:             key = (d.get(\"model\"), d.get(\"condition\", \"W16\"), rid)\n56:             if key in seen:\n57:                 continue\n58:             seen.add(key)\n59:             out.append({\n60:                 \"file\": os.path.basename(f), \"model\": d.get(\"model\"),\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
