{"step_index":192,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T15:01:26Z","thinking":"**Reviewing potential theorem sources**\n\nThe `GraphInvariantsComputable.lean` file appears unhelpful; it contains only two theorems, neither related to the target concepts. Initial search was fruitless.\n\nConsidering other challenge files in the benchmark directory to find potential relevant theorems or patterns. Observed `(nontrivial) ⇒ 2 ≤ sub_total_domination_number` and `(nontrivial) ⇒ 2 ≤ total_domination_number` theorems in two different challenge files.\n\n\n**Evaluating potential contradictions**\n\nInspecting theorems, the hypothesis is that a contradiction may exist within the set of challenges. Focusing on Challenge `a23c41a0`: `(nontrivial) ⇒ order ≤ (2 · edge_cover_number)`.\n\nAnalyzing Challenge `39fd4057`, which states `((nontrivial) ∧ (bipartite)) ⇒ edge_cover_number ≤ independence_number`. In a bipartite graph, the edge cover number is related to the order due to Konig's theorem and Gallai's identity. Thus, further investigation is necessary to determine if a contradiction exists given these constraints.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c \\\"\\nimport networkx as nx\\nfrom graphcalc.graphs.invariants.domination import roman_domination_number, total_domination_number\\n\\nfor G in nx.graph_atlas_g():\\n    if G.number_of_nodes() >= 2 and nx.is_connected(G):\\n        td = total_domination_number(G)\\n        rd = roman_domination_number(G)\\n        if td > rd:\\n            print(f'Counterexample to total_dom <= roman_dom: {list(G.edges())}')\\n            break\\nelse:\\n    print('total_dom <= roman_dom holds on atlas!')\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Check total dom <= roman dom\"","toolSummary":"\"Check total